      "writtenOn": "2023-08-20T23:47:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for testing. For reference, the messages sent are:\n```\n0x84 - REPORT_PHYSICAL_ADDR\n0x87 - DEVICE_VENDOR_ID\n0x82 - ACTIVE_SOURCE (with physical addr \u003d 0.0.0.0)\n0x80 - ROUTING_CHANGE\n0xa0 - VENDOR_COMMAND_WITH_ID\n```\n\nFrom the spec, ACTIVE_SOURCE is usually sent by a source when it wants to become active, but it can also be sent by the TV in this case:\n\n\u003e Note: there is a special case when a TV switches to its internal tuner or to another non-HDMI source (e.g. Y/C, or a SCART socket on European market sets). In this case, it is the TV which broadcasts the \u003cActive Source\u003e message with address 0.0.0.0.\n\nIs there another source connected?",
      "parentUuid": "ced1681d_871ea3db",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 166,
        "startChar": 26,
        "endLine": 166,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "5ada453298dd38231b24dea757d362ce0ddd183d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
